        "id": 1439319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-11-27T16:15:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "apexer creates an unsigned apex. We then use java.Signapk rule on it to create a signed APEX.\n\nWe want to compress a signed apex, so that when we decompress it (we are planning to have apexd decompress directly into /data/apex/active folder), the system will be able to trust it.\n\nUsing --compress flag with apexer will create a compressed APEX with unsigned apex inside it. If we place that in /data/apex/active, system will reject it since it is not signed. (at least that\u0027s my understanding)",
      "parentUuid": "de5997ad_159d11a9",
